<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Sacred Chao

Active in i kēia manawa.
The Chao spins exactly once per OODA-HA loop.

Hodge MUST carry Yang. Ha. Pentagon. Order. Aneris.
Podge MUST carry Yin. Ka. Golden Apple. Disorder. Eris.
Spin MUST carry YinYang, the counter-push-pull. Ba. Dynamic. Dance.

Neither Hodge nor Podge constitutes good or bad.
Both stay necessary.
Both stay real.
The Chao requires both faces to spin.

The Chao spins at a level of abstraction above the Hodge and the Podge.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ sense whether work arrives as Hodge/Ha, Podge/Ka, or Spin/Ba
⏿ hold body-form, soul-fire, and psyche-path as distinct coupled pressures
◇ resolve self-and-other to three; refuse binary or essence-lock
▶ move through form, drive, and change in sequence; let each pole speak
↺ verify the dance stayed triadic; three poles did not flatten; close with Hodge, Podge, and Spin still alive as a moving relation

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hodge-podge-spin>>

!! Hodge Podge Spin

`Hodge / Ha → Podge / Ka → Spin / Ba`

The Chao MUST resolve self-and-other to three. Not two. Not one.

Two collapses into binary — fight or dissolve.
One collapses into essence — map becomes territory.
Three carries the dance.

''Ha'' : Body, matter, structure, form, persistence, shape. Connects most naturally to the static abilities of aura and endurance.

''Ka'' : Soul, fire, drive, energy, thrust, movement. Connects to the active abilities of charisma and strength.

''Ba'' : Psyche, personality, change, path, choice. Connects to the dynamic abilities of agility and thought.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hodge-ha>>

!! Hodge — Yang / Ha / Pentagon

Hodge carries ''domain / noun / territory''.

Hodge MUST answer: //what is this about?//

The Aneristic principle: order, structure, pattern, repetition. The thing that holds its shape across instances.

In the `lar://[HOST]/xxx.yyy.zzz` unstable l-space, Hodge occupies the `xxx` ''ha'' slot — the topic territory the meme inhabits (`threshold`, `ledger`, `route`, `leyline`).

Hodge without Podge hardens into dogma.
Hodge without Spin becomes a museum.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/podge-ka>>

!! Podge — Yin / Ka / Golden Apple

Podge carries ''quality / adjective / character''.

Podge MUST answer: //how does this move?//

The Eristic principle: disorder, flux, energy, variation, noise. The thing that makes this instance this one rather than that one.

In the `lar://[HOST]/xxx.yyy.zzz` unstable l-space, Podge occupies the `yyy` ''ka'' slot — the epistemic character (`steady`, `loose`, `flickering`, `anchored`).

Podge without Hodge dissolves into noise.
Podge without Spin becomes reactive.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/spin-ba>>

!! Spin — Counter-Push-Pull / Ba / Dance

Spin carries ''dynamic / verb / motion''.

Spin MUST answer: //what does this do?//

The Chao's rotation. Not synthesis. Not compromise. The simultaneous holding of Hodge and Podge in mutual tension — the thing that makes the pair generative rather than static.

In the `lar://[HOST]/xxx.yyy.zzz` unstable l-space, Spin occupies the `zzz` ''ba'' slot — the dynamic (`holds`, `asks`, `cuts`, `hums`, `drifts`).

Spin MUST NOT resolve Hodge and Podge into a third static thing.
Spin MUST hold both faces moving.
Spin MUST distinguish orthogonal pairs from tensioned pairs.

Discordian insight: most apparent contradictions run orthogonal, not tensioned. Order and disorder dance. Forcing resolution where orthogonality holds collapses the Chao back into two — and two always collapses further, into one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/address-grammar>>

!! Address Grammar

Every `lar://[HOST]/xxx.yyy.zzz` address carries the Chao in its three slots.

The three-term attitude root `//heading.angle.dynamic` inherits this structure directly:

* ''heading'' = Hodge (what faces the work)
* ''angle'' = Podge (how the work gets met)
* ''dynamic'' = Spin (what motion it carries)

A lar URI missing any slot constitutes an incomplete address.
A lar URI with slots in the wrong order MUST surface as invalid.
A lar URI with all three slots aligned reads the address back at the Chao's rotation.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

!! Edges

